      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T17:04:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When you are saying \"mutex seems to be not needed for real\" do you mean that it is guaranteed that other threads hasn\u0027t yet seen this `command` thus there is no possibility for them to use a stale cached value of this field? I think this is not a safe assumption as CPU caches work in \"chunks\" so a possibility exists that another CPU has already fetched a copy of the chunk containing this `command` in its own cache, and thus without explicit synchronization it will possibly read the stale state of this variable. This will be extremely hard to diagnose. Thread safety analysis exists for a reason :)\n\nI would say that the approach with modifying `mWaitStatus` post-hoc in this method looks hacky to me. It would be better if `mWaitStatus` could be set correctly during creating of `Command` instead. Do you think that is possible to change?\n\nOverall, the CL makes sense to me, thank you for working on it!",
      "parentUuid": "5b78d3dc_f0624b67",
      "revId": "ed69de3222e5e789546f2612096c4f32eed43234",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
